description:
"Sleeping" in Grindelia (gumplant) on an overcast morning along the bayshore. A large colony of Bembix americana was a few meters away.

Not at all sure of ID. Looks a bit like our recent single observation on iNat of a Heterostelis sp: https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/288325317

@dgreenberger @johnascher @umt Tagging you because of the discussion a few months ago on David's observation; perhaps a similar bee? Does this one key out to any of the Stelis sp mentioned by Dr Ascher in comments (S. anthidioides or S. hurdi)?
